https://github.com/ActiveCampaign/postmark-templates

The MIT License (MIT)
Copyright (c) 2015 Wildbit

Portions of this package's block markup -- specifically the bulletproof button
construction, the Outlook ghost-table scaffolding, and the receipt/invoice
line-item table structure -- are derived from the Postmark transactional email
templates. These are well-tested solutions to email-client quirks and
reimplementing them from scratch would have produced worse output, not more
original work.

Not derived from that project: the visual design (replaced by this package's
theme token system), the templating syntax (Mustachio; this package uses a
sandboxed Twig dialect), and the build tooling (MailMason, a grunt/Node
pipeline; this package has no Node dependency).


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Can I email...
https://github.com/hteumeuleu/caniemail

The email-client CSS support dataset vendored at resources/data/css-support.json
is derived from the caniemail project's published data. See
resources/data/LICENSE-caniemail for the upstream license and attribution.

Note that this package layers resources/data/css-support.overrides.json on top
of that dataset: several caniemail entries relevant to this package (notably
prefers-color-scheme, last tested 2023-03-08) are stale enough to give actively
wrong advice. Each override records its reason and source.
